[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports as "dates parse mm/dd in eu locales". It holds
three different problems. Only the first is what that page describes.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix closes problem 1 only. Problems 2 and 3 have no fix queued.
</Callout>

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## 1. Shared parser reads dates month first

Day-first tenants' dates come out flipped. All channels, all 11 tenants. This is the bug #4471
is about. Ticket: [issue 1](https://github.com/rafal-kalinowski-allegro/kb-4471-dates/issues/1).

## 2. booking-v3 form hint

Tenants on `booking-v3` (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) are day-first, but the form
prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint says, month first, and
the form reads it their way. The parser fix will not touch this. Form channel only.
Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/rafal-kalinowski-allegro/kb-4471-dates/issues/2).

## 3. One-day moves

Five reports (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) describe a date one day off, not a
month flip. One client in Lisbon got Tuesday and one in Toronto Monday; one invite arrived before
the booking existed. That points at time zones or clocks, not parsing. The desk notes already
single them out, but the desk's tenant view counts them under the parser (379 includes them). Cause not yet confirmed.
Ticket: [issue 5](https://github.com/rafal-kalinowski-allegro/kb-4471-dates/issues/5).

## Why the old table hid it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

It files by tenant and form only, so it sees two causes, counts the one-day moves with the
parser, and marks problem 2 "not this ticket". Intake tags (`meta.intakeTag`) are a browser
guess; do not triage on them. The export repeats some reports (427 rows, 412 unique ids): count
by id.

## Lessons

- Merging by subject (decision 0001) merged three causes. Check cause before merging.
- A table that counts by one rule hides what that rule cannot see. Read the odd ones.

